WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.453
Step six.

00:00:00.503 --> 00:00:04.313
When the infrastructure is ready, the app workflow starts on its own.

00:00:04.363 --> 00:00:07.846
It builds three images and pushes them to the private registry.

00:00:07.896 --> 00:00:11.154
Then the rollout waits for approval at the production gate.

00:00:12.204 --> 00:00:15.902
Once approved, the job rolls out the release, waits for every deployment,

00:00:15.952 --> 00:00:17.750
and smoke-tests the public endpoint.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.866
The production environment now points to the live URL.

00:00:20.916 --> 00:00:23.854
In the cluster: three deployments, two replicas each,

00:00:23.904 --> 00:00:26.109
with autoscalers and disruption budgets.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:29.078
Only the portal is exposed through a load balancer.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.534
Both AP Is stay internal.

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:34.124
The two nodes run in different availability zones of Indonesia Central.

00:00:34.174 --> 00:00:38.034
And here is Contoso Health: three hundred and sixty members, who has paid,

00:00:38.084 --> 00:00:40.518
who is due by the tenth, and who is in arrears.

00:00:40.568 --> 00:00:44.210
Filter on Not paid, to see members in arrears, and what they owe.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:48.372
Open a member for the details: contribution, payer, months in arrears,

00:00:48.422 --> 00:00:50.156
and a year of payment history.

00:00:50.206 --> 00:00:54.475
The second tab shows free beds per class, across twenty two hospitals.

00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:57.545
And the same per hospital, refreshed every few minutes.

00:00:57.595 --> 00:01:01.045
The info endpoint shows the version, which is the commit, plus the region,

00:01:01.095 --> 00:01:02.890
the cluster, and the pod that answered.
